abstract: "An ongoing mathematical-physics research program developing a falsifiable test architecture for physical-to-experiential bridge claims. The repository formalizes deterministic and stochastic factorization tests, intervention-resolved causal structure, temporal and multiscale compatibility, finite-data certification, target-provenance non-circularity, target-measurement channel robustness, target-channel identifiability, finite-sample target-channel recovery, target-model adequacy and four-view overidentification, finite-sample target-model adequacy rejection, finite-sample full-law model-set separation, certified continuous model-distance lower bounds, quantum operational sufficiency tests, adaptive experiment design, and certified calibration and optimization. Proposition 71 proves that targets constructed as functions or descriptor-only channels of the tested physical descriptor satisfy the corresponding bridge or screening-off condition by construction. Proposition 72 adds the noisy-target layer and proves one-way residual transfer, witness erasure, target-TV contraction, channel-stability bounds, and a conservative finite-sample target-separation certificate. Proposition 73 gives an explicit population inversion for a nondegenerate binary latent target observed through three conditionally independent binary views, identifies the P72 stability coefficients up to the unavoidable latent-label symmetry, and proves by construction that two views do not generally identify individual channel reliabilities. Proposition 74 propagates one simultaneous eight-cell finite-sample confidence event through the P73 inversion, adds a covariance nondegeneracy gate, and gives conservative confidence intervals for the latent target-channel quantities. Proposition 75 separates identifiability from model adequacy: it shows that three binary views are generically just-identified, while a fourth binary view creates six generic overidentifying degrees of freedom, observable covariance-tetrad and cross-triple consistency obligations, a fourth-centered-moment relation, and a full-law reconstruction audit. Proposition 76 propagates one simultaneous sixteen-cell Hoeffding event through denominator-free P75 polynomial constraints to obtain finite-sample rejection certificates for target-model inadequacy; non-rejection remains explicitly inconclusive and is not model acceptance. Proposition 77 upgrades that finite-data adequacy layer to the complete declared model set: if the simultaneous empirical-law confidence region is disjoint from the model family, or a sound lower bound on empirical distance to the model exceeds the same sampling radius, the declared model is rejected at the stated confidence level. Proposition 78 closes the corresponding continuous-model computational gap for the P75 family by exploiting its nine-parameter multi-affine structure: exact-rational parameter-box enclosures provide certified global lower bounds on L-infinity model distance, explicit admissible parameter points provide upper bounds, and an explicit mesh-width bound controls convergence under refinement. P78 preserves the P77 requirement that only a valid lower bound, not an ordinary best-fit upper bound, can certify full-law separation. Proposition 79 adds an exact-rational upper certificate for the P77 sampling radius using rational logarithm bracketing and integer-certified dyadic square-root enclosure, making the final P78/P79 comparison one-sided and rounding-direction safe. Proposition 80 tightens the continuous P75 separation side by intersecting P78 exact cell intervals with the probability simplex and computing the resulting L-infinity relaxation distance exactly in rational arithmetic; the P80 box bound is never weaker than P78 on the same parameter box. Proposition 81 adds exact parameter-box ranges for every nonempty projected binary cylinder event and transfers event-level mismatch back to a full-law L-infinity lower bound through the event-size Lipschitz inequality. The combined P81 box certificate is the maximum of the P80 simplex-coupled bound and the projection-event bound, is never weaker than P80, and can be strictly stronger even when the empirical law lies inside the P80 interval-simplex relaxation. Proposition 82 adds exact nested projection-contrast residual intervals for the same P75 family, audits 256 genuinely new residual events, and yields a never-weaker certificate with an exact-rational strict witness improving P81 from one sixteenth to one twelfth. The downstream calibration branch includes lower-bounded heterogeneous calibration and exact primal-dual gap decomposition through P70. Current documented theorem frontier: P82. The physical-to-experiential bridge remains open, and the project does not assume that consciousness is a scalar, state of matter, quantum variable, or additional spacetime dimension."
